+# VCS Recomp — Native PSP Savedata Utility HLE
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-15  
+**Base:** `PSPRecomp_VCS_NATIVE_GUEST_BOOT_MENU_SOURCE_2026-08-15.zip`  
+**Estimated overall project progress:** **~70%** on the current post-reset/correctness line.  
+**Performance-optimization pass:** unchanged by this revision; this is savedata/frontend correctness work.
+
+## Goal
+
+Remove the rejected Windows/host-created save chooser from the interactive path.
+`LISTLOAD`, `LISTSAVE` and `LISTDELETE` must behave as PSP `sceUtilitySavedata`
+operations and appear inside the same PSP/GE framebuffer that VCS presents.
+
+Important architectural detail: VCS itself requests `sceUtilitySavedata`; on a real
+PSP the screen is owned by the PSP system utility/firmware, not by a VCS-authored
+Game-page renderer. Therefore the correct recomp path is firmware-style HLE in the
+PSP framebuffer. It is **not** a Win32/ImGui/desktop replacement window.
+
+## What changed
+
+### 1. Host save dialog removed from the compiled path
+
+`profiles/vcs/CMakeLists.txt` no longer links `host/savedata_dialog.cpp`.
+The old `savedata_dialog.cpp/.hpp` files are retained only as tiny tombstones so
+extracting this hotfix over an older tree also overwrites/removes the rejected
+Win32 chooser implementation.
+
+The savedata path contains no `choose_savedata_slot()`, `DialogBox` or savedata
+`CreateWindowExW` implementation.
+
+### 2. Asynchronous PSP utility state machine
+
+The existing savedata I/O implementation remains authoritative, but list modes
+now stay active across `sceUtilitySavedataUpdate()` calls instead of blocking on
+a host dialog.
+
+Implemented list modes:
+
+- mode 4 — `LISTLOAD`;
+- mode 5 — `LISTSAVE`;
+- mode 6 — `LISTDELETE`.
+
+Input is edge-triggered from the normal PSP controller sample. The first frame
+latches held input so the button that opened the utility cannot immediately
+activate a slot.
+
+Behavior now follows the PSP utility flow:
+
+- `LISTLOAD`: Cross on a slot starts the load directly;
+- `LISTSAVE`: an empty slot saves directly; an existing slot opens overwrite
+  confirmation, defaulting to **No**;
+- `LISTDELETE`: opens delete confirmation, defaulting to **No**;
+- Left/Right chooses Yes/No in confirmation;
+- Circle/Start backs out;
+- failed operations return to the list so the user can retry;
+- no-data load/delete paths return the savedata error result instead of silently
+  pretending success.
+
+### 3. Savedata screen is emitted into the PSP GE framebuffer
+
+New files:
+
+- `host/savedata_utility_ui.hpp`
+- `host/savedata_utility_ui.cpp`
+
+`ge_renderer.cpp` remembers the real framebuffer descriptor used by ordinary GE
+draws. At display vblank, immediately before the DX12 color frame is finalized,
+`vcs_profile.cpp` asks the utility renderer to compose its frame into that same
+target.
+
+There is no second HWND, taskbar item, popup, GDI canvas or ImGui surface.
+
+### 4. PSP save-list layout
+
+The HLE surface is 480x272 and follows the PSP savedata layout used by the title:
+
+- 480x23 utility banner;
+- selected save image: 144x80 at `(27, 97)`;
+- neighboring saves: 81x45;
+- save-information separator at `(180, 136)`;
+- title, save-title/detail and slot information on the right;
+- Cross/Circle prompts at the bottom;
+- list, confirmation, result and no-data states.
+
+The renderer intentionally does not invent VCS artwork.
+
+### 5. Real `ICON0.PNG` is now used
+
+Existing saves expose their persisted `ICON0.PNG` path through the savedata slot
+record. `savedata_utility_ui.cpp` decodes that PNG in-process with the FFmpeg PNG
+decoder already linked by the VCS profile, converts it to RGBA8 and uploads it as
+a texture to the existing DX12 GE backend.
+
+The selected and neighboring save thumbnails therefore use the **actual PSP save
+icon supplied by the game/save**, not a host-created imitation. If an old save
+has no `ICON0.PNG`, the renderer uses a neutral empty placeholder and never
+fabricates replacement artwork.
+
+### 6. Existing metadata path preserved
+
+The previous correctness work remains intact:
+
+- `VCSNative.meta` sidecar support;
+- standard `PARAM.SFO` fallback;
+- `TITLE`;
+- `SAVEDATA_TITLE`;
+- `SAVEDATA_DETAIL`;
+- save-name list enumeration;
+- actual host save directory/file operations.
+
+### 7. Mouse/keyboard/gamepad ownership
+
+`display_window_set_system_utility_mode()` switches the existing presentation
+window into system-utility input mode while savedata is active:
+
+- desktop cursor visible;
+- camera/fire mouse bindings suppressed;
+- left click -> PSP Cross;
+- right click -> PSP Circle;
+- wheel -> PSP Up/Down;
+- keyboard and XInput continue through the normal PSP button mapping.
+
+This code routes input only; it does not draw savedata pixels.
+
+## Validation completed here
+
+### Source audits
+
+- `check_correctness_0_1.py`: **PASS**
+- `check_frontend_boot_mouse_savedata.py`: **PASS**
+- `check_native_savedata_utility.py`: **PASS**
+
+The dedicated savedata audit checks that:
+
+- the Win32 chooser is unlinked;
+- list modes are asynchronous;
+- utility rendering occurs at PSP vblank into the GE target;
+- save-list geometry is present;
+- confirm/result states are wired;
+- real `ICON0.PNG` decode/upload is present;
+- savedata HWND/dialog calls are forbidden;
+- utility mouse routing is present.
+
+### CTest
+
+**5/5 PASS**:
+
+- `psprecomp_tests`
+- `vcs_profile_tests`
+- `vcs_config_tests`
+- `audio_resampler_tests`
+- `vcs_bootstrap_paths_tests`
+
+The exact `VCSNative` host object files changed by this pass were also compiled
+successfully in the application target (`savedata_utility_ui.cpp`,
+`vcs_profile.cpp`, `ge_renderer.cpp`; `display_window.cpp` was already current in
+the incremental tree).
+
+## Physical validation still required
+
+This environment cannot compile/run the Windows `_WIN32` branch with the user's
+VS2022/Windows SDK/DX12 driver. The next physical test should therefore verify:
+
+1. Game -> Load Game opens the in-frame 480x272 PSP utility, with no desktop
+   popup;
+2. real save thumbnails appear from `ICON0.PNG`;
+3. Up/Down and mouse selection line up with visible slots;
+4. LISTLOAD loads the selected slot directly;
+5. overwrite/delete confirmations default to No and Left/Right select Yes/No;
+6. Circle backs out cleanly;
+7. after load/save/delete, the utility shuts down and control returns to the
+   original VCS frontend/game.
+
+### Remaining visual-fidelity item
+
+The screen currently uses a compact internal bitmap font for system-utility text.
+It is not a Windows font and does not create host UI, but its glyph shapes are
+not yet a byte/pixel recreation of the PSP firmware font. The layout, state
+machine, metadata and real save artwork path are implemented. A later visual
+calibration pass can replace only the glyph rasterizer without changing the
+savedata HLE architecture.
+
+## Build
+
+Keep the existing Ninja build directory. Do not delete it.
+
+```bat
+profiles\vcs\BUILD_VCS_NINJA.bat
+```
+
+The source-list change replaces the old dialog source with
+`savedata_utility_ui.cpp`, so CMake/Ninja will relink the profile as needed.
+
+## Permanent delivery rule
+
+Continue future VCS recomp stages with updated complete source, handoff, patch,
+validation/log summary, hashes, commercial-asset audit and an estimated total
+project progress percentage.
